---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
        title="Terms — Means+Measures"
        description="Terms for using the Means+Measures website."
>
    <section class="section">
        <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>

        <div class="measure">
            <h1>Terms</h1>

            <p>
                The Means+Measures website is provided for informational, publication, archival, and procurement-reference purposes.
            </p>

            <p>
                Published materials should be read in their stated context. Draft, active, archived, and historical statuses indicate publication state rather than legal advice, procurement acceptance, or institutional endorsement by any third party.
            </p>

            <p>
                Public-record artifacts are presented for archival and inspection purposes. External filings, agency records, and linked source materials remain governed by their original record systems and legal contexts.
            </p>

            <h2>Plain language</h2>
            <p>
                Use the public pages to read, cite, inspect, and share Means+Measures material in context.
                Do not use the site to misrepresent authorship, imply endorsement, or remove warnings
                that protect people from relying on stale or incomplete information.
            </p>

            <h2>KC directory data</h2>
            <p>
                KC directory exports are free to mirror, redistribute, repost, quote, transform, and build on.
                Attribution is welcome but not required. Mirrored copies should keep a visible correction
                path because stale resource information can cause real harm.
            </p>

            <h2>Public artifacts</h2>
            <p>
                Public comments, records, and documents may include government material, submitted
                comments, analysis, or source references. Reuse those materials with attention to their
                original legal and record context.
            </p>

            <h2>Accessibility and consent</h2>
            <p>
                If a page, policy, form, or document is hard to use because of language, disability,
                format, or context, contact us. Means+Measures treats accessibility as part of informed
                consent, not as decoration.
            </p>

            <h2>Harmful uses</h2>
            <p>
                Means+Measures does not invite use of its materials for surveillance, discriminatory screening,
                predictive policing, targeted harassment, or systems that make vulnerable people easier
                to punish. Public-interest reuse is welcome. Extractive reuse is not.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
